ivacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:e685a4820801e9b14859a91f6ea43a38be4dc75673a8601904fcc49bd6b6565c","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-17T05:23:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T05:23:54Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1212-v0.12.12/m12stage12-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1212-v0.12.12","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1212-v0.12.12","body":"# Engacer OS M12.12 / 0.12.12 - System tray and quick settings\n\nM12-STAGE12-VM-v1 native qualification passes for these exact bytes. Complete public publication proof closes separately before the next stage.\n\nBuild: `93839018f852f6b6ba79643004d5f101`.\nISO SHA256: `c25247ddc6d38194bd809dae0fe905409056fc45f60946c3c306b0a1c5a4b857`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `274f65cecc047af9a47b141b88737085ff33547935ba6841bba263e8767bce0b`.\n\n## What changes\n\nWindows+A opens one bounded native panel with Quick settings, USB drives and\nCalendar. Wider taskbars show network, USB and audio entries beside the real\nUTC date/time; compact taskbars retain a reachable System button.\n\nNetwork state and retry admission follow the real provider. PCM level/mute\ncontrols the actual software gain and saves for restart when storage is free.\nDuring file work it explains a session-only change. USB Open uses common Files;\nsafe removal checks the actual flush result and refuses during a transfer.\nGeneration-bound controls prevent a held click from targeting a replacement.\nThe real UTC calendar opens the optional Calendar only by explicit choice.\nRemoving Clock, Calendar or Media Player leaves the base services intact.\n\n## How and why\n\nReuse shared controls, original icons and existing kernel providers. There is\nno extra app slot, worker, pixel cache or idle scanner. Fixed shell state grows\nby 239 bytes to 553,196. [Architecture](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a8e035b04e5fb6fad4784d9c821f4d1569cce994/docs/architecture/tray-m1212.md),\n[system tray guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a8e035b04e5fb6fad4784d9c821f4d1569cce994/docs/handbook/tray-m1212.md) and\n[eight-step installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a8e035b04e5fb6fad4784d9c821f4d1569cce994/docs/handbook/install-m1212.md).\n\n## Verification\n\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a8e035b04e5fb6fad4784d9c821f4d1569cce994/evidence/M12/12/acceptance-results.json) binds\n593 compiled inputs and 11 native task/profile checks to real installation,\nUSB/PS2 independent startup, exact saved preferences, local DHCP/link/retry,\nunavailable playback, optional-app removal/reinstallation, late USB replacement\nand a real 64-MiB transfer/cancel/removal guard. Source USB images are unchanged.\nFour real display profiles include compact light/dark and physical 4K/200%.\nExact enabled-device VMware, separate BIOS, twelve movement comparisons and\nactual compressed boot repair pass. The production decoder passes 559 round-trip\npages and 10,808 malformed/fuzz cases with unchanged guards and no heap allocation;\nproduction taskbar arithmetic passes 295,907 host assertions.\n\n[Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a8e035b04e5fb6fad4784d9c821f4d1569cce994/evidence/M12/12/resources.json) distinguish initial hardware,\nfixed state, peak and completed UI retention. Configured guest RAM is not\nmeasured kernel consumption. [Development observations](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/a8e035b04e5fb6fad4784d9c821f4d1569cce994/evidence/M12/12/diagnostics/README.md)\nretain failed harness observations separately from the final passes.\n\n## Scope and retained limits\n\n- A local IPv4 address is not proof of Internet access. PCM gain is not a\n  universal hardware master mixer. Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and battery providers are unavailable.\n- Calendar uses UTC and bounded 2000–2099 navigation; no timezone/DST/NTP claim.\n- Existing filesystem/device, eight-window and create-only USB export limits remain.\n- M12.14 retains feedback/modal arbitration; M12.16 retains scale/cursor work,\n  M12.17 renderer work and M12.18 the BIOS/AHCI observation and complete final\n  controller/original-app matrix. Physical/ARM, vendor GPU 3D and universal\n  Windows compatibility remain unqualified.\n- Agent visual review is not a human study. Public release and full website\n  verification close separately before M12.13.\n\n![Actual native provider-backed system tray](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/a8e035b04e5fb6fad4784d9c821f4d1569cce994/evidence/M12/12/feature.png)\n"}